{
  "id": "fix-stale-search-results-race-in-handlebrowserqu-c50b",
  "title": "Fix stale search results race in handleBrowserQuery",
  "description": "meridian.js handleBrowserQuery() has no ordering guard. Typing \"a\" then \"ab\" fires two concurrent search() calls; whichever resolves last wins, so results for a stale query can overwrite the newer ones. The existing browserSearchActive flag only tracks whether search is active, not which query is current.\n\nFix: capture a monotonically increasing sequence id (or the exact query string) at call time and bail out of renderSearchResults if it is no longer the latest before rendering. Verify by throttling network/CPU and typing quickly that only the final query's results render.",
  "status": "done",
  "priority": "medium",
  "label": "Bug",
